% global_cardinality rule (b) (M7-T24, D-0099): a FORCED value fixes its candidates.
%
% Exactly two of x, y, z take 2, and y + z <= 3 forbids it being those two. The search
% guesses x = 1 first (indomain_min): that leaves exactly two candidates for the two 2s,
% and rule (b) fixes both y and z to 2 -- both bounds of each, from the count's `>=` row --
% before int_lin_le refutes the branch. The learned clause rests on those pushes. x = 2
% then needs one more 2 out of y and z, and y = 1 makes z the last candidate, which rule
% (b) fixes again. SAT, every line checked (D-0053).
var 1..3: x :: output_var;
var 1..3: y :: output_var;
var 1..3: z :: output_var;
constraint fzn_global_cardinality([x,y,z],[2],[2]);
constraint int_lin_le([1,1],[y,z],3);
solve :: int_search([x,y,z], input_order, indomain_min, complete) satisfy;
